WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
I'm really worried. You only have 5

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.720
years left to get rich. You see, the gap

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.240
between the rich and the poor is growing

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.640
and every year you wait, it gets harder

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.480
and harder to close. Over the next 5

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.880
years, the people that have money and

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.960
assets will continue to get richer, but

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:20.120
those that haven't accumulated any could

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:23.160
find themselves stuck in the same

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:25.680
economic position forever, effectively

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.520
frozen in time. That's exactly why I had

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.840
to make this video. You'll notice

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.840
there's no polish editing or fancy props

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.240
today. That's because this subject is an

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.360
emergency warning and I need to get this

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.320
video out fast. Look,

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.000
I'm an old man. I've seen many

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.120
transformational shifts throughout my

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.120
lifetime that have completely changed

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:46.680
the way money gets made. Every time

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:49.000
there was a shift, people had to adapt

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.040
and those who didn't got left behind.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.040
But here's the thing, none of those

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.640
shifts ended up replacing humans

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.120
themselves. [music]

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.640
However, now,

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.160
for the first time in my lifetime, I've

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.400
started to question whether that will

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.720
still be true because we're seeing the

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:07.120
biggest technological shift I've ever

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:09.560
witnessed, which is of course AI. So,

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:13.520
that brings me back to why do you only

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.520
have 5 years left to get rich?

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.560
Every job and business exists because

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.560
there's a problem that needs solving.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.720
Think about it. A company needs somebody

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.760
to answer its phone, so it hires a

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.400
receptionist. It needs somebody to sell

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:28.600
its product, so it hires a salesperson.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.800
It needs somebody to manage the

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:33.320
finances, edit promotional videos, or

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.840
design packaging. There's a problem that

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:37.960
needs solving and a human gets paid to

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.960
solve it. Now, for most normal people,

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:41.440
the problem they've traditionally solved

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:43.480
has been through their job. You might

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.560
not own property or a company or have

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:47.480
stocks and millions sitting in the bank,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.240
but you could always sell your time,

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:51.080
knowledge, and skills. And that was a

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:53.040
way of moving up the ranks and getting

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:55.000
rich, but it wasn't always like that.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.960
For most of human history, if you were

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.120
born into a wealthy family that owned

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:01.040
land and assets, you'd almost certainly

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:03.479
remain wealthy. And if you were born

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:05.120
poor, there was a good chance you'd stay

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:07.240
poor. That's because the people at the

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.679
top owned the assets, and the people at

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:12.400
the bottom worked for them. The only way

00:02:09.679 --> 00:02:14.440
to cross the divide was to marry up, and

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.760
even then, they'd look down on you for

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.040
it. Then businesses and the free market

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:21.080
knocked a hole in that wall, and every

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.560
shift I talked about earlier knocked it

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:26.200
down a bit further, until social media

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:28.320
finally smashed it into smithereens. But

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:30.480
the more I think about it, the more I

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.400
feel like AI could start pushing us in

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.560
the opposite direction. You see, if

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.480
people get paid to solve problems, what

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.400
happens when AI starts solving those

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.400
problems instead? What happens when a

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.000
company no longer needs five people to

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:45.040
do a job because an AI agent can do all

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.440
the work itself. Those problems don't

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.360
disappear, but far fewer humans get paid

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.720
to solve them. And if the main thing you

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:53.360
own is your ability to sell your time,

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.720
but the value of that time starts

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.480
falling, building wealth becomes a lot

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:59.080
harder. Meanwhile, the person who

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.800
already owns the company gets the

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:03.959
opposite. Their cost drop, their output

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.760
goes up, and they keep the difference.

00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:07.280
And that's the part that worries me,

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.360
because those walls that block any

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.080
movement from poor to rich could slowly

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.160
start being rebuilt. And when that

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.200
happens, you end up stuck on whichever

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:18.200
side of the wall you happen to be on at

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:20.160
that time. Look, I started this YouTube

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:23.000
channel to help people build wealth from

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:24.920
scratch, just like I did, as I believe

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:27.480
that anyone who learns the skills of a

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.920
millionaire can become a millionaire.

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:31.920
That's why I'm so worried, because AI is

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.640
attacking my whole reason for making

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:35.840
videos in the first place. And this

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:39.800
isn't just theory anymore. We're already

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:39.800
starting to see the warning signs.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.640
Nobody wants [music] to hear this, but

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:45.680
the entry-level jobs that used to be the

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:47.400
first step on the ladder are the first

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.800
ones disappearing. And I'm not talking

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:52.400
about some far-off prediction here.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.240
Anthropic, one of the big AI companies,

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.000
looked at how Claude was actually being

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:57.640
used out in the real world. They found

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.920
that Claude is now being used for at

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:02.920
least a quarter of all tasks in roughly

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.120
half of all jobs. Just a year earlier,

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:07.640
it was only around a third of jobs. And

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:10.400
remember, that's just Claude. It doesn't

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:12.200
even include ChatGPT or any other AI

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.200
tools people are using. And this is

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:15.920
where it gets uncomfortable. Stanford

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.959
have been looking at actual payroll

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.120
records covering millions of workers,

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:23.280
and they found that employment among 20

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:26.400
to 25-year-olds in the jobs most exposed

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:28.280
to AI is now about 19% below where it

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.640
would have been if they kept pace with

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:32.560
young workers in less exposed jobs. In

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:34.480
addition to this, older, more

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:37.680
experienced workers in those highly

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:39.280
exposed jobs don't show the same gap.

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.560
So, think about what that actually

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:43.240
means. The people already inside and

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:45.880
making loads of money are largely

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:48.120
holding onto their jobs. Well, at least

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:50.240
for now. But, fewer new places are

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:52.760
opening up underneath them. And if you

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.360
just looked at the overall job market,

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:56.520
you might miss it because that same

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.720
Stanford study found no evidence of

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:01.240
widespread job displacement across the

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.240
economy, which is exactly why hardly

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:05.240
anybody is doing anything about it. And

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.440
while all of that's going on, something

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.480
else has been happening in the

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:10.280
background. In America, the share of

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.800
business profits that actually goes back

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:14.919
